From: abrus861 <abrus861@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:33:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] bluez5: backend-native: keep the transport when AT+BCS
 confirms the current codec

Backport to PipeWire 1.0.5 (Ubuntu 24.04) of the fix proposed in
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/pipewire/pipewire/-/issues/5506 and shipped in
https://github.com/abrus861/pipewire-hfp-atbcc-fix (patches/0003, written for
1.6.x). 1.0.5 frees and re-creates the transport inline instead of calling
rfcomm_new_transport(), otherwise the logic is identical.

Some headsets (HUAWEI FreeClip/FreeBuds Pro 5, Poly Voyager Legend 50) send
AT+BCC on every audio connection after the first one, shortly after the AG
has started the eSCO connect. The AG answers +BCS:<current codec>, the headset
confirms with AT+BCS=<same codec>, and the handler then (a) frees and
re-creates the transport and (b) emits codec_switched, which makes the device
remove and re-create its nodes. Both close the SCO socket while its connect
is still in progress.

The kernel answers the close with Create Connection Cancel, which does not
cancel an eSCO setup; the controller completes the link anyway and the host
has no connection for it. The link is now orphaned ("SCO packet for unknown
connection handle") and every later Setup Synchronous Connection to the
headset is refused (0x20 "Unsupported LMP Parameter Value" on MediaTek
MT7925, 0x0a "Synchronous Connection Limit to a Device Exceeded" on Intel)
until the ACL link is reconnected.

If the confirmed codec is the one already in use and a transport exists,
there is nothing to switch: reply OK and keep the transport and the nodes.
---
 spa/plugins/bluez5/backend-native.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/spa/plugins/bluez5/backend-native.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/bluez5/backend-native.c
@@ -911,10 +911,22 @@ static bool rfcomm_hfp_ag(struct rfcomm *rfcomm, char* buf)
 			return true;
 		}
 
-		rfcomm->codec = selected_codec;
-
 		spa_log_debug(backend->log, "RFCOMM selected_codec = %i", selected_codec);
 
+		if (rfcomm->transport != NULL && rfcomm->codec == selected_codec) {
+			/* The headset re-confirmed the codec that is already in use (some headsets send
+			 * AT+BCC on every audio connection).  Keep the transport: freeing it here would
+			 * close a SCO socket whose connection may still be in progress, which leaves an
+			 * orphaned eSCO link in the controller and breaks all later SCO setups.
+			 * For the same reason no codec_switched event is emitted: the device would
+			 * remove and re-create its nodes, releasing the transport mid-connect. */
+			spa_log_debug(backend->log, "RFCOMM codec unchanged, keeping transport");
+			rfcomm_send_reply(rfcomm, "OK");
+			return true;
+		}
+
+		rfcomm->codec = selected_codec;
+
 		/* Recreate transport, since previous connection may now be invalid */
 		if (rfcomm->transport)
 			spa_bt_transport_free(rfcomm->transport);
